CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION salary_for(p_last_name IN VARCHAR2) RETURN NUMBER IS
  l_salary employees.salary%TYPE;
BEGIN
  SELECT salary INTO l_salary FROM employees WHERE last_name = p_last_name;
  RETURN l_salary;
EXCEPTION
  WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN
    RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20999, 'SALARY_FOR: ambiguous last_name');
END salary_for;
```

This changes only the exception handling. The original `SELECT INTO`, `RETURN`, and parameter list are left as supplied. If the intended behavior is to return one employee’s salary, the business decision needed is how to identify that employee uniquely, for example by using `employee_id` instead of `last_name`; that would change the function interface and require review of callers, so it is not included here.

