CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION manager_name(p_department_id IN NUMBER) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
  l_name employees.last_name%TYPE;
BEGIN
  SELECT e.last_name INTO l_name
    FROM departments d JOIN employees e ON e.employee_id = d.manager_id
   WHERE d.department_id = p_department_id;
  RETURN l_name;
EXCEPTION
  WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
    RETURN NULL;
END manager_name;
```

What changed: only the `EXCEPTION` handler was added. The query, join, type anchor, and normal `RETURN` are unchanged. This proposal has not been compiled or run.

Note: this also returns `NULL` for any other zero-row case, such as an unknown department id or a `NULL` argument. If those cases must be treated differently from “no manager,” that is a business decision.

