    Check 2: a non-NULL department_id that should match no rows.

    The candidate is a fixed negative value, then confirmed with COUNT(*).
    If it is not actually absent from the table, this check reports FAIL and
    counts as a failure because the setup found no suitable no-match key.
  */
  l_no_match_department_id := -999999999;

  SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO l_expected
    FROM harness_app.employees
